IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa13-regulative.l4: the duties of Part 17 (ss 549 to 609) that name a party and, where the text gives one, a time limit, written as
-- regulative rules (PARTY ... MUST / SHANT ... WITHIN ... HENCE ... LEST ...). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- Each duty is ALSO encoded as a decision function in the chapter modules (coa13-ch2-allotment.l4 and so on), and those functions are
-- the ones the tests ASSERT: a DEONTIC value cannot be compared with EQUALS in an #ASSERT, so a regulative rule is run with #TRACE
-- (coa13-tests-regulative.l4) and its outcome is read from the printed Result block, not counted (NOTES.md, "What the stable binary
-- does not accept").
--
-- THE CLOCK. WITHIN counts days on the trace's clock. Where a section counts months or days from a date, the rule takes that date as an
-- input and WITHIN is the number of days from it to the last day the section allows, so a trace stamped AT 0 starts on that date.
-- Only the party named by the text is an actor, and the actions are declared here under the coa13 prefix, not in the core.
-- What a failure leads to is only what the text states: an offence (named in a comment) or a liability; no remedy is invented.

§ `Part 17: the duties that name a party`

DECLARE `coa13 duty of the company` IS ONE OF
    `s 554(1) the company registers the allotment of shares`
    `s 555(2) the company delivers the return of allotment to the registrar`
    `s 556(2) the company delivers the return of allotment of the new class to the registrar`
    `s 578(2) the company repays the money received from applicants`
    `s 597(1) the company delivers a copy of the valuer's report to the registrar`
    `s 602(1) the company delivers a copy of the resolution and the valuer's report to the registrar`
    `s 549(1) the company's directors exercise the power to allot shares or grant rights`
    `s 552(1) the company applies its shares or capital money in payment of a commission, discount or allowance`
    `s 561(1) the company allots equity securities without making the pre-emption offers`
    `s 562(4) the company withdraws the pre-emption offer before the end of its period`
    `s 580(1) the company allots shares at a discount`
    `s 578(3) the directors repay the money with interest`

-- ---- the duties with a time limit (MUST ... WITHIN) -----------------------------------------------------

-- src:7668 | (1) A company must register an allotment of shares as soon as practicable and in any event within two months after the date of the allotment.
@ref s 554(1) a company must register an allotment within two months after the date of the allotment (src:7668)
GIVEN `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `coa13 duty of the company`
`s 554(1) the duty to register the allotment` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 554(1) the company registers the allotment of shares`
    WITHIN (Day (`add months` `the date of the allotment` 2)) MINUS (Day `the date of the allotment`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the allotment was not registered within two months after the date of the allotment (an offence by the company and by every officer in default: s 554(3))"

-- src:7679 | (2) The company must, within one month of making an allotment of shares, deliver to the registrar for registration a return of the allotment.
@ref s 555(2) the company must within one month of making an allotment deliver a return of the allotment (src:7679)
GIVEN `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `coa13 duty of the company`
`s 555(2) the duty to deliver the return of allotment` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 555(2) the company delivers the return of allotment to the registrar`
    WITHIN (Day (`add months` `the date of the allotment` 1)) MINUS (Day `the date of the allotment`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the return was not delivered within one month of the allotment (an offence by every officer in default: s 557(1))"

-- src:7694 | (2) The company must, within one month of making such an allotment, deliver to the registrar for registration a return of the allotment.
@ref s 556(2) the unlimited company must within one month of making such an allotment deliver a return (src:7694)
GIVEN `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `coa13 duty of the company`
`s 556(2) the duty to deliver the return of allotment of the new class` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 556(2) the company delivers the return of allotment of the new class to the registrar`
    WITHIN (Day (`add months` `the date of the allotment` 1)) MINUS (Day `the date of the allotment`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the return was not delivered within one month of the allotment (an offence by every officer in default: s 557(1))"

-- src:7879 | (2) If shares are prohibited from being allotted by subsection (1) and 40 days have elapsed after the first making of the offer, all money received from applicants for shares must be repaid to them forthwith, without interest.
-- src:7880 | (3) If any of the money is not repaid within 48 days after the first making of the offer, the directors of the company are jointly and severally liable to repay it, with interest at the rate for the time being specified under section 17 of the Judgments Act 1838 (c. 110) from the expiration of the 48th day.
@ref s 578(2) the money must be repaid forthwith once 40 days have elapsed; s 578(3) if not repaid within 48 days the directors are jointly and severally liable (src:7879-7880)
GIVEN `the date of the first making of the offer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `coa13 duty of the company`
`s 578(2) the duty to repay the money received from applicants` MEANS
    -- The 40 days after which repayment is due "forthwith" cannot be written as a window that opens (AFTER is rejected on the stable
    -- build); the rule runs to the 48th day, the day by which the text makes the directors liable; the decision function
    -- `s 578(2) the company must repay ...` says from when the duty is owed.
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 578(2) the company repays the money received from applicants`
    WITHIN 48
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY Director
        MUST `s 578(3) the directors repay the money with interest`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "the directors are jointly and severally liable to repay the money with interest from the expiration of the 48th day; the defence in s 578(3) is the director's own proof that the default was not due to his misconduct or negligence"

-- src:8072 | (1) A company to which a report is made under section 593 as to the value of any consideration for which, or partly for which, it proposes to allot shares must deliver a copy of the report to the registrar for registration.
-- src:8073 | (2) The copy must be delivered at the same time that the company files the return of the allotment of those shares under section 555 (return of allotment by limited company).
@ref s 597(1) the company must deliver a copy of the valuer's report to the registrar, at the same time as the return of allotment (src:8072-8073)
GIVEN `the day the company files the return of allotment under section 555` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `coa13 duty of the company`
`s 597(1) the duty to deliver a copy of the valuer's report to the registrar` MEANS
    -- The clock starts on the day the return is filed and the copy is due on that day (the same time: fork F-597(2)).
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 597(1) the company delivers a copy of the valuer's report to the registrar`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the copy of the valuer's report was not delivered at the same time as the return of allotment (an offence by every officer in default: s 597(3))"

-- src:8130 | (1) A company that has passed a resolution under section 601 with respect to the transfer of an asset must, within 15 days of doing so, deliver to the registrar a copy of the resolution together with the valuer's report required by that section.
@ref s 602(1) a company that has passed a resolution under s 601 must within 15 days deliver a copy with the valuer's report (src:8130)
GIVEN `the date on which the company passed the resolution` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `coa13 duty of the company`
`s 602(1) the duty to deliver a copy of the resolution and the valuer's report` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 602(1) the company delivers a copy of the resolution and the valuer's report to the registrar`
    WITHIN 15
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the copy of the resolution and the report were not delivered within 15 days (an offence by the company and by every officer in default: s 602(2))"

-- ---- the prohibitions (SHANT) --------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7608 | (1) The directors of a company must not exercise any power of the company—
-- src:7609 | (a) to allot shares in the company, or
-- src:7610 | (b) to grant rights to subscribe for, or to convert any security into, shares in the company,
-- src:7611 | except in accordance with section 550 (private company with single class of shares) or section 551 (authorisation by company).
@ref s 549(1) the directors must not exercise the power except in accordance with s 550 or s 551 (src:7608-7611)
GIVEN `s 549(1) the directors are prohibited from exercising the power` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `coa13 duty of the company`
`s 549(1) the directors' duty not to exercise the power` MEANS
    IF `s 549(1) the directors are prohibited from exercising the power` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Director
         SHANT `s 549(1) the company's directors exercise the power to allot shares or grant rights`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "the directors exercised the power without authority under section 550 or section 551 (an offence by a director who knowingly contravenes it: s 549(4))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:7652 | (1) Except as permitted by section 553 (permitted commission), a company must not apply any of its shares or capital money, either directly or indirectly, in payment of any commission, discount or allowance to any person in consideration of his—
-- src:7653 | (a) subscribing or agreeing to subscribe (whether absolutely or conditionally) for shares in the company, or
-- src:7654 | (b) procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions (whether absolute or conditional) for shares in the company.
@ref s 552(1) a company must not apply its shares or capital money in payment of a commission, discount or allowance (src:7652-7654)
GIVEN `s 552(1) the company is prohibited from applying its shares or capital money in payment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `coa13 duty of the company`
`s 552(1) the company's duty not to apply its shares or capital money in payment` MEANS
    IF `s 552(1) the company is prohibited from applying its shares or capital money in payment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Company
         SHANT `s 552(1) the company applies its shares or capital money in payment of a commission, discount or allowance`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company applied its shares or capital money in payment of a commission, discount or allowance not permitted by section 553"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:7730 | (1) A company must not allot equity securities to a person on any terms unless—
@ref s 561(1) a company must not allot equity securities to a person unless it has made the pre-emption offers (src:7730)
GIVEN `s 561(1) the company is prohibited from allotting the equity securities to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `coa13 duty of the company`
`s 561(1) the company's duty not to allot equity securities without the pre-emption offers` MEANS
    IF `s 561(1) the company is prohibited from allotting the equity securities to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Company
         SHANT `s 561(1) the company allots equity securities without making the pre-emption offers`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company allotted equity securities without making the offers required (the company and any officer who knowingly authorised or permitted it are liable to compensate: s 563(2))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:7750 | (4) The offer must state a period during which it may be accepted and the offer shall not be withdrawn before the end of that period.
@ref s 562(4) the offer shall not be withdrawn before the end of the period during which it may be accepted (src:7750)
GIVEN `the number of days from the day the offer is made to the last day of the period during which it may be accepted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `coa13 duty of the company`
`s 562(4) the duty not to withdraw the pre-emption offer` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    SHANT `s 562(4) the company withdraws the pre-emption offer before the end of its period`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the day the offer is made to the last day of the period during which it may be accepted`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the offer was withdrawn before the end of the period during which it may be accepted (a contravention of section 562 for the purposes of section 563)"

-- src:7898 | (1) A company's shares must not be allotted at a discount.
@ref s 580(1) a company's shares must not be allotted at a discount (src:7898)
GIVEN `s 580(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited because it is at a discount` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `coa13 duty of the company`
`s 580(1) the company's duty not to allot shares at a discount` MEANS
    IF `s 580(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited because it is at a discount` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Company
         SHANT `s 580(1) the company allots shares at a discount`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the shares were allotted at a discount (the allottee is liable to pay the company the amount of the discount with interest: s 580(2))"
    ELSE FULFILLED
